Initial P07 trajectory observation — retained for comparison, not a controlled
runtime-memory conclusion.

This was the first 4,000-transform implementation sample, run before the
checked-in `wp8_probe.py` existed. It used the same temporary-BREP framework
worktree setup and a small local construction counter, but did not explicitly
delete every returned placement or run `gc.collect()` at sample points.

    transform count    retained entries    VmRSS KiB
                100                 100       513380
                512                 512       519360
               1000                 512       526288
               2000                 512       540424
               4000                 512       568412

    placement constructions including working-set warmup: 4003
    trajectory elapsed seconds: 0.5297304549894761
    three-transform working-set requests: 12
    three-transform working-set hits: 9

The retained-entry plateau at 512 is valid P07 evidence. The increasing RSS
must not be attributed to one particular runtime/allocation cause: the later
checked-in probe differs by fresh-process control, explicit deletion, and
forced collection. Both samples are retained so that this distinction remains
visible to review.
